{"title":"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Forum_Threads\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Forum Threads</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also:</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given two fixed, distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, find the locus of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> belonging to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that the quadrilateral formed by point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the centroid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> (in that order) can be inscribed in a circle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_1\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07fb197df7bb042844b9d1eac083956ce2cf577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f38d8c69777a0bdce430ec7ae8fd6be1f6c7561.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3x+1}{y+z}+\\frac{3y+1}{z+x}+\\frac{3z+1}{x+y}\\ge\\frac{4}{2x+y+z}+\\frac{4}{x+2y+z}+\\frac{4}{x+y+2z},\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"41\" />\nwith equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1bb32241472c525e5624db47ff8edf81dd33a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_2\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>At a certain (lame) conference with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> people, each group of three people wishes to meet exactly once. On each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days of the conference, every person participates in at most one meeting with two other people, with no limit on the number of groups that can meet. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01c92774786a323f661eea8764e0a3b00c6351fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min d$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> for\n</p><p>a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4f171162b090bab7ce5dfa1c58715850530ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3d24ab7a9d144a9306246d14fe57d153c4194f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_i\\}_{i\\ge0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a16f2d4ee29c282b705559743af4c40867c16c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b2594dfaaf361922def54df426c59b1cbcb55e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}(n-i)a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"136\" height=\"50\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that for all nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06680560f45154435d2abdab7989041f23ae055f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{m}\\frac{a_k}{4^k} &lt; \\frac{9}{5}.\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all solutions to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/993d98166fac2a34470d5ee92cea1b9994512731.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5\\cdot4^{3m+1}-4^{2m+1}-1=15n^{2m},\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In convex, tangential quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, let the incircle touch the four sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/15991b3141a86264dede361a307e9d9e1753d4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC, CD, DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aeae5cdffa852d1d28cb919190626dc0a28baf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, F, G, H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, respectively. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/7644daf8dcab57e0450b7476727f68e230771bd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[EFGH]}{[ABCD]} \\le \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"43\" />\n<b>Note:</b> A tangential quadrilateral has concurrent angle bisectors, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f631f7a53d834de52b718ed6b496689e9658eadf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[X]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the area of figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Forum_Threads\">Forum Threads</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Forum Threads\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h345916p1850492\">Initial Discussion</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h345916p1850492\">Problems PDF</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h345916p1858538\">Solutions PDF</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also:\">See Also:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_USAJMO\" title=\"Mock USAJMO\">Mock USAJMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Past_Contests\" title=\"AoPS Past Contests\">AoPS Past Contests</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194003\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 197/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5843/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8912:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194003 and revision id 70920. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}